WEBVTT

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:10.570
<i>This is the Forest Cup in Oarai's 
Sun Beach's final round.</i>

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:12.510
<i>Start the heat.</i>

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.990
<i>Akitsuki Sho and Tanaka Nalu.</i>

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.650
<i>The time limit is 30 minutes.</i>

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.850
Sho-sama, and Tanaka-kun! You can do it!

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.000
We're rooting for both of you!

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:34.630
Sho-sama! Nalu!

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.930
<i>Priority goes to Tanaka.</i>

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.310
<i>He's waiting for a wave.</i>

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.930
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:33.960
Wave 4

00:02:29.230 --> 00:02:34.000
<i>It's an offshore wind leading 
to strong, slightly wild breaks.</i>

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.160
<i>If he catches a good wave, will he be able 
to complete three maneuvers?</i>

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.640
Tanaka.

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.010
Thank you for making it 
all the way to the finals.

00:02:44.550 --> 00:02:47.640
It's not something you need to thank me for.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.510
After all, I've always wanted to have a 
serious showdown with you just once.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.270
Full-out.

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:57.280
Full-out.

00:02:58.010 --> 00:03:00.810
<i>We have just hit the 22 minute mark.</i>

00:03:00.810 --> 00:03:03.590
<i>We still haven't had a good set come in.</i>

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:08.410
<b>Sho-sama

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:07.550
If he can ride one, it'd be the third here.

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:10.370
The wind seems to have calmed a little.

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:13.290
<b>Sho-sama

00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:13.290
They might get some good waves.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.300
<b>Sho-sama       Fight!</b>

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:18.300
<b>Nalu     Fight!</b>

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:15.690
Sho-kun!

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:18.300
Tanaka-kun, we're rooting for you too!

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:22.600
<i>Tanaka has made his move.</i>

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.650
<i>Take off!</i>

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.400
<i>He delivered that beautifully!</i>

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.360
<i>The spray really flew on that!</i>

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.830
<i>He took that wave and showed us 
a ride in the 7-point range!</i>

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.330
Tanaka! You're looking good!

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:52.800
<i>Now, Akitsuki is making his move.</i>

00:04:07.490 --> 00:04:09.220
<i>He picked a good wave...</i>

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.110
<i>This is sure to be in the 7-point range, too!</i>

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.730
<b>Sho-sama                            Fight!</b>

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.730
You're looking very cool!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:19.900
You live up to your title, Sho-sama!

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.240
Stunning!

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:25.480
<i>Now, the second run. 
Priority goes to Akitsuki.</i>

00:04:27.580 --> 00:04:29.310
You're not going for that one?

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.750
Didn't seem like it would run the whole way.

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.250
Seriously. You've got keen eyes.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.630
The longer you wait, the more you feel 
like there's a good wave coming, right?

00:04:40.070 --> 00:04:41.470
Yeah.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:47.770
<i>Take off!</i>

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:56.880
<i>This second run might have 
the best scores of the day!</i>

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:02.030
Way to go! I expect nothing less!

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:04.450
Go!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.550
<i>Tanaka looks undaunted.</i>

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:12.790
<i>He caught a wave with great potential!</i>

00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:15.960
<i>There just isn't a point gap 
between their scores!</i>

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.310
Hinaoka-kun, you look pale.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:26.670
I didn't realize... 
I-I'd forgotten to breathe.

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.040
Are you okay?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.300
I-I'm fine.

00:05:31.150 --> 00:05:33.930
They don't have much time left.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.940
The next run might be their last chance.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:38.440
Sho...

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.510
Tanaka...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.190
<i>Now, the swell has started to get bigger.</i>

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.030
<i>Tanaka has secured himself priority.</i>

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.040
<i>Now, he's waiting for a set. 
Three minutes remaining!</i>

00:06:06.940 --> 00:06:08.640
<i>Here comes a wave!</i>

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:10.340
<i>But he lets it pass!</i>

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:15.850
<i>He passes on another one!</i>

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:17.800
He's not moving.

00:06:17.800 --> 00:06:19.140
He's waiting.

00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:23.770
Nalu knows Oarai's ocean really well.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:28.740
He'll wait until the very last
second for a good wave.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.360
When you get swells coming in like this,

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.010
what follows is...

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.620
<i>They have 30 seconds left.</i>

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.380
Here it comes!

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.880
<i>Here's the hottest wave of the day!</i>

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.390
No. It's the best this year!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.140
<i>Tanaka is on the move.</i>

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.000
<i>Akitsuki follows!</i>

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:02.830
<i>At this rate, they risk running 
out of time. All they can do is go!</i>

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:07.130
<i>The next wave is a big one, too!</i>

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:10.150
Let's go!

00:07:38.530 --> 00:07:39.890
Now!

00:08:11.230 --> 00:08:14.490
<i>And that's the end of the competition!</i>

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:22.660
<i>Both surfers showed us a great battle.</i>

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:39.370
<i>Now, who will get the win?</i>

00:08:39.990 --> 00:08:41.560
Brilliant.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:44.590
I have no other way to express it.

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.620
Yeah.

00:08:45.950 --> 00:08:50.850
The seventh episode of <i>Magical Maid Miruru</i>, 
"Miruru Meets her Mother in Heaven"...

00:08:50.850 --> 00:08:52.590
This moved me nearly as much as that!

00:08:53.710 --> 00:08:57.700
That was amazing. 
Sho-kun and Tanaka-kun, both.

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:56.160
You were amazing! Amazing!

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:58.890
Sho-sama!

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.090
I see.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:04.970
What do you think, Rindo-kun?

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.300
Of what?

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:11.780
The coming of new rivals. 
Doesn't it make you think?

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:15.370
Rivals? To whom are you referring?

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:16.860
All of them.

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:23.570
They are members of our surfing world 
who will shake things up and make it exciting.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:29.060
If you say so, Bill. Perhaps 
I'll hold out a little hope for them.

00:09:40.220 --> 00:09:43.660
Yes. Please have high hopes for them.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.540
Sho! Tanaka!

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:07.710
Guys, seriously...

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.880
I love you both!

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:11.250
Hey! Seriously?

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:12.710
Corgi!

00:10:45.030 --> 00:10:46.700
Sho-sama...

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.250
Tanaka-kun, you were cool, too!

00:10:50.180 --> 00:10:53.510
I'm so proud that you're my students.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:55.260
I'm proud you're my customers.

00:10:58.120 --> 00:11:01.910
<i>I wasn't the least bit upset.</i>

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:04.600
<i>I mean, why would I be?</i>

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:07.210
<i>There was too big 
a difference in our levels.</i>

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:11.180
<i>It made me want to try much, 
much harder at surfing.</i>

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.520
<i>I wanted to get much, much better at it.</i>

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.590
<i>So much more.</i>

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:22.970
It probably won't take too long

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:26.160
for Akitsuki-kun to become a surfer 
who will represent Japan.

00:11:26.160 --> 00:11:27.590
That's true.

00:11:27.590 --> 00:11:30.340
Competing in world competitions 
might not be just a dream.

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:31.920
Just like Sally.

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:34.520
Right. Just like Sally...

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:36.420
Sally?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:39.920
Sally started in the Magical Kingdom,

00:11:39.920 --> 00:11:42.300
then she spread her wings 
and flew off to see the world!

00:11:43.200 --> 00:11:45.460
Flew off to see the world...

00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:50.930
from Oarai... to a world competition?

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:55.480
World...

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.190
World, huh?

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.660
Okay! I've made up my mind!

00:12:00.870 --> 00:12:02.870
I'm going to aim for the world stage, too!

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.700
Sho and I will enter 
a world competition together!

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.710
If you want to laugh, go ahead. I just...

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.740
We won't laugh.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:14.700
Huh?

00:12:15.320 --> 00:12:18.420
Because we feel the same way.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.220
I can't say that I hate that kind of thing.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:25.220
In that case, we're rivals, right?

00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:27.230
Yes, we are.

00:12:27.230 --> 00:12:28.070
Yeah.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:39.640
Sho... Tanaka!

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.100
We heard you, Masaki.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.020
A world competition?

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.740
Count me in, too.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.740
But you're a free surfer, aren't you?

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.570
Yeah, but...

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:56.750
After being in today's competition, 
I think this kind of thing might not be so bad.

00:12:59.000 --> 00:13:00.670
And me.

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.210
You wouldn't leave me out, would you?

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:06.470
Looks like you're doing something fun.

00:13:06.470 --> 00:13:08.510
Huh? Kosuke-san.

00:13:08.840 --> 00:13:10.650
You came?

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:12.650
I had nothing else to do.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.120
Um...

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:15.840
I'm a surfer, too.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:19.180
In that case, let's all do this!

00:13:19.180 --> 00:13:20.400
Yeah.

00:13:21.610 --> 00:13:27.200
<i>After this, we all really did aim 
for world competition.</i>

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:29.500
<i>With our friendly rivalry spurring us on...</i>

00:13:31.430 --> 00:13:33.760
<i>We became irreplaceable friends.</i>

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.420
Let's all aim for it! For the world!

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:45.430
Yeah!

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.790
Just like Sally!

00:13:47.790 --> 00:13:49.820
Okay. Let's go!

00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:51.180
Go where?

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:53.540
The ocean, of course!

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.750
Summer will never end! Come on!

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.520
Surfing...

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:20.080
Let's do it!

00:14:27.510 --> 00:14:32.760
"The miserable have no other 
medicine. But only hope."

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:36.380
The only medicine that 
works on unhappiness is hope.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:38.890
This is a quote from Shakespeare.

00:14:39.670 --> 00:14:43.670
This will appear on your test... probably.

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.280
Or it may not.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.670
Are you going to get a new wet suit?

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.210
I was thinking about it, but...

00:15:09.210 --> 00:15:11.550
They really are expensive, aren't they?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.040
Once I get accepted into a high school, 
I'll have to get a part-time job.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.630
Masaki-kun!

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.330
Have you decided where 
you're going for high school?

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:22.940
Well... Not yet.

00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:27.820
But you have to turn in your application 
right after New Year's, don't you?

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:33.200
Yeah. It'd be nice to go to high 
school here in Oarai with Sho, but...

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.430
Yuta-kun and the others 
from Shonan invited you,

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:39.700
saying, "Won't you come to
high school with us," right?

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.010
Right.

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:43.330
That's why... I'm still not sure 
what I want to do.

00:15:43.330 --> 00:15:47.280
The ocean is Shonan is really nice!

00:15:47.280 --> 00:15:49.840
The waves are different 
from the ones here in Oarai.

00:15:50.300 --> 00:15:52.470
And that makes it so much fun.

00:15:53.130 --> 00:15:55.760
I was so happy back then.

00:15:56.470 --> 00:16:01.000
Life... is just like choosing 
the right waves.

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:09.530
<i>An incredibly powerful low pressure system 
is currently headed north.</i>

00:16:09.990 --> 00:16:13.490
<i>Tonight and tomorrow are likely 
to bring heavy storms.</i>

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:16.490
It's so cold!

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:19.530
To be or not to be...

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:23.500
Oarai or Shonan, that is the question.

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.680
What's that supposed to be?

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:29.000
It's Shakespeare. He said it was 
going to be on the test, didn't he?

00:16:30.610 --> 00:16:35.010
Sho... You're going to stay in Oarai, right?

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:39.310
Yes. I don't know about the future,

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:41.230
but for now, for high school.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:43.720
They invited you too, Sho...

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.250
You should just go to high school in Shonan.

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:53.960
For Sho... Shonan is...

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:53.040
You can just pipe down, Murphy.

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:59.170
If I could go to Shonan, 
I'm sure it would be fun, but...

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.910
It isn't that easy.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.040
What?

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:07.420
Nothing. Never mind.

00:17:08.070 --> 00:17:10.660
Well, let's do a little more.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.350
Yeah!

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.500
Wait up, Sho!

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.440
What is it, Corgi? Sighing like that...

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:35.450
Every time you sigh, 
a little happiness runs away.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:40.490
Before aiming for the world stage,

00:17:40.490 --> 00:17:43.510
I have to decide which 
high school to aim for...

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:46.460
Somehow, that feels harder.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.690
What do your mom and dad say?

00:17:49.690 --> 00:17:53.890
Both my mom and my dad say, 
"You should do what you want, Masaki."

00:17:53.890 --> 00:17:55.470
They would say that.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:59.730
Your family really is wonderful, Masaki.

00:17:59.730 --> 00:18:01.220
I wish I had one like it.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.670
It isn't really "wonderful."

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:06.870
It's just normal, you know? Normal.

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.980
This is just my opinion, but...

00:18:09.690 --> 00:18:14.800
I think maybe "normal" is
actually a really happy thing.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.740
I wish I'd been born 
into a normal household.

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:27.360
No matter where you decide 
to go to school, Masaki,

00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:29.500
I'll support that decision.

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:34.550
Even if it's Shonan, it won't be goodbye.

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.290
We're connected by the ocean.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:40.310
Besides...

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.440
Besides?

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.580
You're still aiming for it, right?

00:18:44.580 --> 00:18:46.520
For the world with the rest of us.

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:48.540
The world...

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:50.000
Yeah.

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:56.030
I want to enter a world competition 
with both of you, Masaki and Tanaka.

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:57.670
So do I!

00:18:58.270 --> 00:19:01.530
No matter where we are, 
our feelings are one.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:10.040
1 new message

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:12.190
Isokichi! Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:19.710
It's so cold! I wish I could 
stay in the bath forever!

00:19:19.710 --> 00:19:22.040
Hawaii is warm all year round, right?

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:25.780
Aloha oe... oe...

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:28.300
You and Sho should come hang out sometime.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:30.800
Let's ride some big waves out there.

00:19:31.240 --> 00:19:33.590
Yeah! I can't wait!

00:19:33.590 --> 00:19:35.440
Right, Sho?

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:39.440
Sho?

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.580
Sho!

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:44.700
Oh! What is it?

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.950
Is something wrong?

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:52.710
It's nothing.

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.460
Come on. Let's head home.

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.240
Well... I'll leave you here.

00:20:27.820 --> 00:20:31.240
Masaki, Tanaka, see you tomorrow.

00:20:32.230 --> 00:20:34.280
Yeah. See you tomorrow.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:37.450
See you tomorrow, Sho!

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:39.250
No! Out in the world!

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:42.260
Out in the world.

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:49.320
This is really impossible...

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:51.080
The snow hurts!

00:21:51.420 --> 00:21:53.820
Isokichi! Let's go home!

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:55.950
Isokichi!

00:22:01.140 --> 00:22:02.170
What is it?

00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:54.800
Wave 5     Beyond That Wave
